    {
     "text": "\\begin{tabular}{@{}l@{}}For $y_i = \\beta_0 + \\beta_1 x_i + \\varepsilon_i$,\\ show that the slope through the two end points is unbiased with variance $2\\sigma^2/(x_n - x_1)^2$,\\ and that\\\\least squares' is $\\sigma^2/\\sum_i (x_i - \\bar x)^2$;\\ which is smaller?\\end{tabular}",
