   "duration": 37.233291666666666,
   "text": "All of it comes back. Cross-entropy, gradients and curvature are how every network in Parts 9 and 11 is trained, and the softmax is logistic regression with many classes. Part 7 builds the statistical models: principal components, mixtures, Bayes. Part 8 asks why a model generalizes at all, and meets the neural tangent kernel, a network that behaves like a kernel machine. Part 13 reads attention as a kernel smoother, and Part 31 asks the same question of language models that we asked of naive Bayes: are its probabilities honest?",
